{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"beton-inversive-stag","creation_channel":"cli","description":"MCP containers start through launch paths that take NO deploy mutex, so the\nautodeploy `flock` cannot be relied on to serialize anything the entrypoint does.\n\nEvidence (found while remediating Gerrit 2244 / d467-e2fc-fd64-49ae):\n\n1. `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:324` — the `mcp:` service is `restart: always`\n   and mounts `gerrit_mcp_tickets:/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets` (line 399), the SAME\n   named volume `mcp_run_new` mounts (`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:370`). A docker\n   daemon restart, host reboot, or crash-loop re-runs the ENTRYPOINT with no flock.\n   The compose file itself (lines 391-393) documents an expected crash-loop when\n   `mcp-static-tokens.json` is absent.\n2. The compose service pins host 8091, which is inside the managed port pool\n   {8091, MCP_PORT_A, MCP_PORT_B} with `MCP_RELEASES_CAP=3`\n   (`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:129,136`), so it can coexist with blue/green\n   containers on the same volume.\n3. Operator runbook restarts (`infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md`) are a further\n   unserialized launch path.\n4. Even WITHIN autodeploy the flock does not cover provisioning: it is backgrounded\n   and outlives the tick (/health answers before the store exists — see the separate\n   open bug mobile-groovy-badger), so the 2-minute timer can start a second container\n   while the first is still cloning.\n\nRe-clone concurrency specifically IS now handled: 2244 adds a hard-link lock in\n`infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh` covering clear+clone across containers. This ticket\ntracks the RESIDUAL, more general risk: the deploy mutex is not a serialization\nguarantee for the entrypoint, so any FUTURE entrypoint step that mutates the shared\nvolume must carry its own serialization, and nothing currently enforces or documents\nthat expectation.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- The unserialized launch paths above are documented where an author of the entrypoint\n  will see them (entrypoint header comment and/or an infra runbook), stating that the\n  deploy flock does not serialize entrypoint work.\n- A decision is recorded on whether the compose `mcp:` service should keep\n  `restart: always` on 8091 while blue/green containers manage the same volume, or be\n  reduced to a boot-only backend.\n- If the answer is that further steps need serialization, the lock is factored so a new\n  step can reuse it rather than re-inventing one.","id":"1890-7d05-eabc-4ac1","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["infra","mcp","concurrency"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP entrypoint launch paths bypass the autodeploy deploy mutex"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787773101245614001,"uuid":"9f80b3f8-1a30-4143-8528-6a99e48b7dbd"}